# Black\-Box Web Application Penetration Test

**Engagement:** GetJunoway Web Application
**Assessment:** Black\-Box Web Application Penetration Test
**Status:** In Progress
**Environment:** Kali Linux
**Focus:** External attack surface, authentication, and access control

---

## Executive Summary

This case study documents an authorized black\-box security assessment of
the GetJunoway web application\. The engagement is being conducted from
the perspective of an external attacker without source\-code access or
pre\-established application credentials\.

The initial assessment phase focused on reconnaissance, authentication
architecture, route discovery, and unauthenticated access\-control
validation\. Testing identified a Next\.js application using Supabase for
authentication and discovered an administrative route at `/admin`\.

Direct unauthenticated requests to the administrative route were
analyzed to determine whether protected content could be accessed
without a valid session\. Although the route was externally discoverable
and initially returned application content, further response analysis
identified Next\.js redirect behavior directing unauthenticated users to
`/login?next=/admin`\.

At the current stage of the engagement, no administrative authentication
bypass has been confirmed\.

---

## Scope & Assessment Approach

The application was assessed externally using black\-box methodology\.
Testing performed to date has included:

- Public application reconnaissance
- Technology identification
- Authentication\-flow analysis
- HTTP request and response inspection
- Route discovery
- Administrative endpoint validation
- Unauthenticated access\-control testing
- Browser and command\-line traffic analysis

The engagement remains in progress, and this case study will be updated
as additional attack surfaces are assessed\.

